21 of 22 mutants killed, all by the testbench's own checks; M17 is equivalent (below).

First run: M16 (the clamp after damping, made too high) survived. U13's 8x8/2 controller was meant to start
above K_MAX but took k_fixed(8, 2, 10, TIGHT), which is 12, and its epoch 0 was damped only by chance. It now
starts at 19 and epoch 0 always damps (B7_precheck.log section 7); M16 run again: killed, 72 errors.

M17 (the sums shifted in from cycle 2N - 1 instead of 2N) is equivalent: the shift register takes one more
bit, the zero that the tree's last node sends in cycle 2N - 1, and that zero leaves the register again with
the last bit, so the controller sees the same sums. Tile (0, 0) sends nothing before its window (cycle 2N), in
U13's stimulus and in the mesh. The mutant in the design-D mesh, 4x4:
  M17 mesh: RESULT CT01-CT05 PASS checks=9043644 errors=0 seed=1
  M17 mesh full: RESULT CT01-CT05 PASS checks=11075837 errors=0 seed=1
  The delivered RTL gives the same counts: 9,043,644 with +QUICK and 11,075,837 in full.

